    {"claim": "A per-inference log captures the unfiled decision the instant it's made, before any victim perceives it and before any claim exists — that's the stopper Safetyist demanded.", "speaker": "Accelerationist", "an_id": "AN-17", "grounding": [{"node_id": "saf-desires-003", "why": "Safetyist's pre-deployment equity demand turns on prevention BEFORE deployment, not detection during; a log that fires 'while the model is live' documents harm that has already reached a person"}, {"node_id": "risk_existential", "why": "for irreversible-harm domains, an ex-post record of a decision already executed is not a halt — the irreversibility is the whole point of precautionary gating"}]},
    {"claim": "The logged-inference layer binds regardless of whether the domain was named in advance, because behavior is captured and available for retrospective review when a novel harm surface shows itself.", "speaker": "Accelerationist", "an_id": "AN-20", "grounding": [{"node_id": "saf-desires-003", "why": "this is the crux the assignment targets: retrospective definition of a novel harm surface is by construction AFTER irreversible damage; Safetyist's precautionary commitment requires specification before the harm is legible"}, {"node_id": "regulation_precautionary", "why": "directly names the value at stake — restricting deployment until safety is demonstrated, which a retrospective log cannot deliver for genuinely novel capabilities"}]},
